{"_id":"wmGMGuide0000001","name":"Wrathmaker — GM Companion","ownership":{"default":0},"pages":[{"_id":"wmGuidePage00001","name":"GM — Settings & campaign overrides","type":"text","sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":0},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>GM — Settings &amp; campaign overrides</h1><p>Wrathmaker · GM reference</p></header><p>This companion is not player-facing. Keep its compendium and imported journal restricted. The Player Guide is safe to share at Observer permission; do not grant players Owner permission to GM notes.</p><p>Open Wrathmaker's control panel in Module Settings. The experimental Workbench is default-off; enable it when ready. Material rules, gathering and Hexploration have separate controls. Disabling a feature preserves saved selections. Enhanced flanking is permanent.</p><p>Edit material names, six-tier values, prices, rarities and bonus types; edit dragon colors and resistance values separately. Edit profession specialisations and their Signature, Mastery and Legacy descriptions. The Player Guide is a shipped default reference, not a live mirror of custom settings: annotate an imported copy when changing campaign rules.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00002","name":"GM — Resources, regions & awards","type":"text","sort":200000,"ownership":{"default":0},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>GM — Resources, regions &amp; awards</h1><p>Wrathmaker · GM reference</p></header><p>Set the gathering reward destination and the fallback environment and maximum Tier. Region-aware gathering can use supported scene/region terrain and level data; verify availability before play. Put mount and vehicle Actors in Wrathmaker Travel's Animals & Mounts and Vehicles & Transport folders.</p><p>Award Resource Units using the resource compendium. Do not halve their base prices merely to perform a half-price sale. Older Treasure documents are preserved; take care with existing project reservations before replacing stock. Apex items are campaign rewards whose prices are intentionally unspecified.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00003","name":"GM — Custom items, recovery & adjudication","type":"text","sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":0},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>GM — Custom items, recovery &amp; adjudication</h1><p>Wrathmaker · GM reference</p></header><p>The GM Item Creator creates world items without project costs. Use typed maker names, compatible Marks and Anchors. Exceeding Capacity requires confirmation; the one-free-Mark restriction still applies.</p><p>Recover Missing Item recreates a completed project's missing output without charging again, while checking for an existing output. Recovery is blocked after dismantling. Do not use recovery to award duplicates.</p><p>Mark automation remains partial. Confirm unspecified activation costs, target selection, limited uses and GM-approved effects before play. Native Mark Actions are rules/chat entries, not proof an effect has resolved. Do not assume structure or Kingdom benefits affect personal equipment.</p><p>The module does not itself define Nephilim Point powers. Define awards and expenditures for your campaign. Back up the world before broad changes to inventory or campaign configuration.</p></section>"}}]}
